# 🛣️ AI Road Damage Detection System

An AI-powered web application that detects **road damages such as potholes, cracks, and surface distress** using a YOLO object detection model.  
The system allows users to upload a road image and automatically identifies damages with bounding boxes and confidence scores.

---

## 🚀 Features

- Upload road images
- Detect potholes and road damage using YOLO
- Display bounding boxes on detected damage
- Show detection confidence scores
- Download the annotated result image
- Simple and interactive web interface using Streamlit

---

## 🧠 Technologies Used

- Python
- YOLO Object Detection
- Ultralytics
- Streamlit
- OpenCV
- NumPy
- Pillow

---

## 📂 Project Structure


image_classifiction/
│
├── app.py # Streamlit application
├── model/
│ └── best.pt # Trained YOLO model
│
├── runs/ # YOLO training outputs
│
├── requirements.txt # Required Python libraries
└── README.md # Project documentation


---

## ⚙️ Installation

### 1️⃣ Clone the Repository


git clone https://github.com/yourusername/road-damage-detection.git

cd road-damage-detection


---

### 2️⃣ Create Virtual Environment


python -m venv yolo_env


Activate it:

Windows

yolo_env\Scripts\activate


Mac/Linux

source yolo_env/bin/activate


---

### 3️⃣ Install Dependencies


pip install -r requirements.txt


Or manually:


pip install ultralytics streamlit opencv-python numpy pillow


---

## ▶️ Run the Application


streamlit run app.py


Then open in your browser:


http://localhost:8501


---

## 📸 How It Works

1. User uploads a road image
2. YOLO model analyzes the image
3. The system detects road damages
4. Bounding boxes and confidence scores are displayed
5. User can download the result image

---

## 📊 Example Output

Detected damages will appear with bounding boxes and confidence scores on the uploaded image.

